  "body": "**The request (mkinney, 2026-11-15):** \"Can we group the user guide main section better?\"\n\nThe guide index (`site/content/guide/_index.md`) and its sidebar list about 25 pages flat by weight: install, first-run, setups, workholding, seven operation pages, posting, refusals, troubleshooting, cli, mcp, glossary and others. A new user cannot see the order of a job, and an experienced user cannot find a page quickly.\n\nWanted: sections that follow a job, for example:\n1. **Getting started:** install, first run, keyboard and mouse.\n2. **Set up the job:** model import, setups, stock, work offsets, workholding, tools.\n3. **Operations:** an overview page, then 2D, 3D, holes and probing, turning, plasma/laser/waterjet, EDM.\n4. **Check and post:** simulation and verify, order of operations, posting, machines and posts.\n5. **Multi-axis:** (the existing section).\n6. **Automate:** CLI, scripting, MCP and AI agents.\n7. **Reference:** units and coordinates, glossary, refusals, troubleshooting, migrating.\n8. **CAM fundamentals:** (the existing section).\n\nUse zola sections (folders with `_index.md`), keep every existing URL working (`aliases` in the front matter), and fix all internal `@/` links.\n\nDone means: the sidebar shows the sections in this order, no old URL returns 404 (redirect aliases), `zola build` passes with no broken links, and the guide index gives a one-line \"start here\" path.\n",
